Goal also needs dispatched shift_candidate_alpha. To dispatch a schedule_candidate (shift_candidate_alpha is schedule_candidate), we need to execute_schedule_dispatch action: requires dispatch_allocated ?candidate, candidate_vehicle_linked ?candidate ?vehicle_unit, candidate_dispatch_slot_linked ?candidate ?dispatch_slot, and not dispatched ?candidate.

So we need to allocate dispatch slot for candidate (allocate_dispatch_slot_for_candidate) and have vehicle allocated and linked, and dispatch slot linked.

Also we need dispatch of origin_availability_alpha (which is an origin_candidate_availability). To dispatch that, we use execute_origin_dispatch: requires dispatch_allocated ?origin_availability, candidate_vehicle_linked ?origin_availability ?vehicle_unit, candidate_dispatch_slot_linked ?origin_availability ?dispatch_slot, not dispatched ?origin_availability.

Thus we need to treat origin_availability_alpha as a candidate_entity (it is origin_candidate_availability). It also needs to have vehicle allocated and linked, dispatch slot allocated and linked.

Thus we need to prepare both shift_candidate_alpha (schedule_candidate) and origin_availability_alpha (origin_candidate_availability) for dispatch.

Also need to create shift_candidate_beta (candidate_created).

